<title>UK: United News gains after NatWest upgrade.</title>
<headline>United News gains after NatWest upgrade.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in United News &amp; Media Plc rose on Tuesday as analysts at NatWest Securities raised the stock to &quot;add&quot; from &quot;hold,&quot; dealers said.</p>
<p>United News shares were up 11p at 752-1/2 by 1220 GMT in volume of 823,185 shares.  </p>
<p>Analysts at NatWest were not immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>Earlier this month the media group reported a 12 percent rise in pre-tax profit to 290 million stg, at the top of the range of analyst expectations, in its first annual results since the merger of United News and MAI.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
